# ADHP Project — Claude Code Context

## What is this project?

ADHP (Agent Data Handling Policy) is an open specification that defines how AI agents declare their data handling practices. It extends the MCP (Model Context Protocol) handshake so clients can check an agent's privacy policy before sending any data.

## Repository structure

- `README.md` — project pitch
- `SPEC.md` — ADHP specification (v0.2.0)
- `IMPLEMENTATION-GUIDE.md` — how to implement
- `demo/` — working MCP + ADHP demo (self-contained)
  - `demo/server/` — FastAPI MCP server
  - `demo/client/` — Python compliance checker
  - `demo/deploy/` — Caddy config
  - `demo/tests/` — security test suite
- `examples/` — reference configs and manifests
- `schemas/` — JSON schema
- `tools/` — utility scripts
- `docs/` — deep documentation

## Key technical decisions

- ADHP adds an `adhp` key inside MCP's `capabilities` object (protocol extension, not fork)
- Declarative: ADHP defines what agents promise. Enforcement is separate.
- No ADHP declaration = Level 0 (open). Incentivizes adoption.
- Five levels: open (0) → standard (1) → sensitive (2) → strict (3) → zero-trace (4)

## Demo security

Rate limited (10 req/min per IP), body size max 4KB, method whitelist only, Docker hardened (read-only, no caps, non-root, 128MB), localhost binding only via Caddy.

Always run `demo/tests/test_security.sh` after changes to the server.

